    "question": {
      ":question/id": "9bb2aa85-4790-5113-a036-3cdac36d03bb",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 8$ matrix. If $B=\\{{b}_{1}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=8,$ and since $B$ is formed by $1$ vector, $\\text{rank}(A)=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 1+\\text{nullity}(A) & =8 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =8-1 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
