      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=5,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. \n\nAlso, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+3 & =5 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =5-3 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
